--Methods / Funtions--

a method is a block of code that we can write once and call whenever we need it.


public static void display()
access modifier: public - means that the method can be accessed from anywhere in the program.
class member: static - means that the method belongs to the class rather than an instance of the class.
return type: void - means that the method does not return any value.
method name: display - is the name of the method, which is used to call it.

public static void display(){
    ....//Method Body
}

Rules

1. Method must be declared inside a class.
2. Method cannot be declared inside another method.
3. Method must have a return type (void if it does not return any value).
4. Method name should follow the camelCase naming convention.
5. () contains parameters (if any) that the method can accept. If there are no parameters, it will be empty.
6. {} contains method statements that define what the method does.
7. Execution starts from main().


